<title>USA: Bonn's resolve on reform strenghened by G7 - Rexrodt.</title>
<headline>Bonn's resolve on reform strenghened by G7 - Rexrodt.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks with other Group of Seven countries has reinforced Germany's resolve to implement domestic structural reform, German economics minister Guenter Rexrodt told a breakfast briefing Saturday.</p>
<p>Rexrodt said after talks with finance and economics ministers from other G7 nations, &quot;The summit discussions have given us strength domestically to pursue structural reforms.&quot;</p>
<p>He cited such issues as increased labor market flexibility and reform of pension and welfare systems.</p>
<p>German is grappling with needs to reform its overregulated labor market to make its companies more competitive and reduce its near-record unemployment.</p>
<p>((--Janet Northcote, Summit Newsroom +1 303 454 8244))</p>
